though). \n\nWhen we got to our hotel, problem arise. Tv did not work. I called the receptionist, and the technician came after an hour later. They tried their best to fix tv, unfortunately the problem was much bigger than they expected. The sad part was they KNEW the tv was broken already and Ritz didn't even solve the problem. (Technician told me our previous guest also had the same problem - broken tv). So, me just being me, asking for a compensation for the broken tv. The technician was very generous giving us $100 restaurant fee.  And I took it with my grateful heart. \n\nResort wise; this property again has a lot activities that you can do with your kids, partners, etc. Hiking by the beach is the most popular activities done by my people. Biking around the area also a great thing to do. \n\nDuring check out time, there was a bit problem since I wanted to redeem the $100 certificate that the technician gave me. A bit miscommunication happened at that time, but they resolved it quickly.\n\nWould I recommend you guys to stay here? if you have $1000 extra to spare for staying a night here, sure you should. \nDon't forget to add\nParking vallet is $53 a day\nResort fee is $50 a day. (that's why maximise the property since you're charged hefty for resort fee). \n\nOther than that, yes I would stay again here. Hopefully I can bump this review to 4 star next time."
